File-based routes live in `src/routes`. The TanStack Router Vite plugin watches them, generates `src/routeTree.gen.ts`, and automatically code-splits route components; run development or a bundle build after adding or renaming a route, and do not edit the generated tree directly. The overview loader primes the shared TanStack Query cache before rendering, while Query owns freshness and the one-retry policy. The status query passes its cancellation signal through both `/api/version` and `/health/ready` requests to the Vite proxy.

A full `scripts/jig dev` session supplies the current backend through `JIG_DEV_API_ORIGIN`, which takes precedence over an inherited generic override. For a direct Vite start or `scripts/jig dev --app <frontend-name>` against a separately managed backend, set `API_ORIGIN`. Authentication is intentionally project-owned; add it at the root route/provider boundary before exposing privileged operations.

Jig generates the real-backend Playwright starter for product SPA roles only. This admin role ships Vitest coverage for its API boundary and overview behavior; add a package-local Playwright suite when the project defines its privileged browser flows and authentication contract.

`index.html` applies the stored or system theme before React starts to avoid a color flash. The inline bootstrap is deterministic so a strict Content Security Policy can authorize its hash; alternatively, replace it with your deployment's nonce-based bootstrap.
